  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Some contributions contain several pieces intended to be claimed as one set; bags, ties, trays, and matching labels are available for display.\", \"decision\": \"How should pieces of a complete set remain together?\", \"goal\": \"Help usable household goods reach interested neighbors while keeping contributions, claims, and final collection understandable.\", \"problem\": \"Neighbors are organizing a one-day fair for clean, usable household goods that people no longer need. Giving and taking are both optional, and no payment or matching contribution is required. Volunteers have intake space, category tables, reserve shelves, a holding area, carts, and simple item records. Contributors choose in advance whether unclaimed goods should be returned during the closing collection period or donated through an arranged pickup.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nVolunteers bag or tie each complete set together before it reaches the display table, leaving its description visible. Visitors handle a single bundle, reducing the chance that pieces from one contribution become separated during browsing.\nVolunteers place each complete set on a dedicated tray and attach one label listing all included pieces. Visitors can inspect the components individually while the tray and inventory show what must leave together.\nVolunteers attach matching set labels to every component and display the pieces within one marked table area. Larger or awkwardly shaped sets remain inspectable, and the repeated identifier helps collectors verify that all pieces accompany the claim."
    }
  ],
